# ThomasTheDaemonEngine Project Context

ThomasTheDaemonEngine (or simply "the Engine") is a fully qualified BPMN 2.0 Workflow Engine built with Elixir/OTP, Ash Framework, Phoenix, and PostgreSQL 16+. It is structured as an Elixir umbrella project following DDD domain boundaries with a strict dependency direction: Core never calls API, Peripheral never blocks Core.

## Key Invariants

- **`EvilEngine.Api`** (Ash Code Interface) is the single shared service layer — every wire adapter and every plugin converges here.
- **Core domains** (`core_types`, `core_execution`, `core_events`, `core_timers`, `core_expressions`, `core_bpmn`) never import from API or Peripheral domains.
- **Plugins** are in-BEAM OTP apps. They call `EvilEngine.Api.*` directly — no HTTP round-trip. There is no gRPC sidecar host.
- **EngineEventBus** is the only channel through which observability, audit logging, and external integrations see engine events.

## Umbrella App Layout

| App | Domain | Purpose |
|-----|--------|---------|
| `core_types` | Core | Behaviour-free structs, shared types |
| `core_execution` | Core | PI/FNI runtime, resume, payload cap |
| `core_events` | Core | EngineEventBus, pending sweeper |
| `core_timers` | Core | ISO 8601 scheduler |
| `core_expressions` | Core | FEEL evaluator |
| `core_bpmn` | Core | XML parser, ModelCache, linter gate |
| `peripheral_persistence` | Peripheral | Ash + AshPostgres, Mix `evil.retention.purge` |
| `peripheral_telemetry` | Peripheral | :telemetry counters, /stats |
| `peripheral_plugins` | Peripheral | Plugin registry, in-BEAM loader |
| `api_auth` | API | JWT validation |
| `api_facade` | API | `EvilEngine.Api` service-layer facade |
| `api_web` | API | REST + GraphQL + WebSocket + Admin |

## Documentation (read on demand, not upfront)

When working on a specific subsystem, consult the relevant docs as needed — do not read all of them before every change:

- `docs/architecture/index.md` — Detailed architecture topics
- `docs/Architecture.md` — High-level overview + layer-by-layer reading guide
- `docs/decisions.md` — Significant A-vs-B choices that still explain the architecture
- `docs/Glossary.md` — Every term used in this project
- `docs/Schema.md` — Database ER diagram

`docs/poc/ImplementationPlan.md` and `docs/poc/ImplementationPhases.md` are archival. Do not treat them as the decision log or the phase tracker.
